This is an independent implementation of a network protocol, produced by
analysing how an existing client program communicates, for the purpose of
interoperability. It contains no code, artwork, audio or text taken from
KONAMI's software. It does contain two small tables of integers, read
mechanically out of the client's data files because a server cannot
arbitrate this protocol without them: the targets of the scenario
branches it has to decide, and, for the lesson quiz, how many questions
each category holds together with which of two answers is right for the
true-or-false ones. Neither table carries any question, any answer text,
or any other text or imagery, and neither is of any use without a
lawfully obtained copy of the game. Message names, map names and
structure offsets appear here because they are the identifiers the
protocol itself uses.

